+### Correcting a booked visit
+
+<a id="req-visitedit-001"></a>
+
+A booked visit can be corrected afterwards. Its date and its description can both be changed, and the correction replaces the values on that visit rather than adding a second visit to the pet `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]`. The correction starts from a form already carrying the visit's current date and description. A correction is held to the same rules as booking: the description must be filled in, and the date must be later than today. A refused correction returns to the form; an accepted one confirms by showing the owner's record. Cancelling a visit remains out of scope (NG-5).
+
+Nothing in the interface points at the correction form in this slice. It is reached by its address alone, and no page offers a link to it `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]`. Whether it gains a visible entry point is an open question the owner has deferred.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a booked visit, when its correction form is opened, then the form carries that visit's current date and description.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a booked visit, when a description and a date later than today are submitted, then that visit carries the new values and the owner's record is shown.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a pet with one visit, when a correction to that visit succeeds, then the pet still has exactly one visit.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a blank description, when the correction is submitted, then it is refused, the description is named, and the form is shown again.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a date of today or earlier, when the correction is submitted, then it is refused, the date is named, and the form is shown again.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given any page of the system, when it is rendered, then it offers no link to the correction form.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A correction addressed to a visit that is not the named pet's is refused rather than shown. This mirrors the booking rule; see edge case 1 of Visits.
+2. A visit whose date has already passed can be corrected only by moving it to a future date. The booking rule applies unchanged — the narrowest reading, recorded as an open question.
+
+**ADR:** [ADR: Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope, Cancelling Is Not](adr/2026-08-15-non-goal-visit-correction-narrowing.md)
+
